# FSD + Figma HTML Pipeline — System Context (.cursor only)

Authoritative process docs live **under `.cursor/`** (this file + agent + skills + rules).

## Purpose

Stage 0: **FSD (source of truth)** + **Figma HTML (UI/nav assist)** → use cases → Excel in Milestone`N` Test Cases (**create if missing, reconcile/update in place if present**) → **mandatory FSD coverage matrix + TC delta + feature delta (for `*_New` / revised sources) + overall % + module/feature breakdown** → gate → `qa-automation-pipeline` → Playwright under `tests/milestoneN/`.

## Priority

| Source | Role |
|--------|------|
| FSD `.docx` | Requirements, rules, expected results, use-case scope |
| Figma HTML | **This run’s** UI flows, navigation, clicks, field labels, modals, action order for Test Steps |

**Behaviour / expected-result conflicts → FSD wins.**  
**Click paths / control labels → follow this run’s Figma** (discover flows; do not assume a fixed catalog or another module’s labels).

## Folder layout (canonical)

```
pipeline/test-data/Milestone<N>/   # N = 1 or 2 (default 2)
  FSD/           # place / select FSD .docx files (optional *_New revisions)
  Figma/         # place / select Figma HTML files (optional *_New revisions)
  Test Cases/    # created or reconciled Excel workbooks
```

User **names** which files to use each run, **or** Stage 0 auto-prefers `*_New` when both a baseline and `_New` sibling exist for the same stem. Do not auto-pick an unrelated file when multiple modules exist without confirmation.

**Input contract:** exactly **one active** FSD `.docx` + **one active** Figma HTML per run. Optional **baseline** siblings (same name without `_New`) are used only for **feature delta**. Do not ask the user to split sources. Inventories under `results/fsd-figma-pipeline/` are machine outputs.

## Revised sources (`*_New`)

| Pattern | Meaning |
|---------|---------|
| `Module_FSD_New.docx` | Revised FSD — **active** source of truth for this run |
| `Module_FSD.docx` | Baseline sibling — used to compute feature add/remove/update |
| `figma_stem_New.html` | Revised Figma — **active** UI for Test Steps |
| `figma_stem.html` | Baseline Figma — optional UI change notes |

When `_New` is active (or a baseline inventory exists), emit `feature-delta-report.json` and display **Feature changes** in the Excel delivery reply. Excel still reconciles the **same** module workbook. On **Approve Excel**, QA pipeline **reconcile** updates Playwright specs for add+update and removes retire IDs.

## Excel mode (create vs reconcile)

| Excel at named path | Mode | Behavior |
|---------------------|------|----------|
| Missing | `create` | Write new workbook from FSD use cases |
| Present | `reconcile` | Update **same** workbook in place: **revise all required columns** for retained TCs, add missing, flag retire orphans; preserve Test Case IDs; `.bak` before overwrite. `keep` only after proven zero-drift column audit. |

Always emit `results/fsd-figma-pipeline/<resultsKey>/tc-delta-report.json`. Removals finalize only after **Approve Excel**.

## Anti–resource-exhaustion (agent work shaping)

Does **not** change the Excel quality bar (atomic TCs, Figma steps, 100% coverage, Shared Quality when §6 in scope).  
Applies to **all** Milestone1/2 modules. **Do not** add per-module Stage 0 generators under `pipeline/scripts/`.

| Do | Don't |
|----|--------|
| Extract once → use `fsd-inventory.json` / `html-inventory.json` | Whole-file `Read` of Figma HTML or FSD into the model |
| Grep / small offsets for exact labels | Stuff entire HTML into context before writing Excel |
| Update `use-cases.json` + Excel by FSD section, then refresh coverage + delta | One giant `Write` of the full TC catalog |
| Keep requirements/TCs in agent Stage 0 artifacts only | Commit `generate-<module>-stage0*.cjs` (or similar) as lasting helpers |
| On child `resource_exhausted`, continue section-chunked in parent | Stop and ask the user to restate or re-upload sources |

