## Trigger

```
Process FSD + Figma HTML from Milestone2
FSD: <FsdFileName.docx>
Figma: <FigmaFileName.html>
Test Cases: <OutputWorkbook.xlsx>
```

Or `from Milestone1` / `Milestone: 1` for Milestone1 roots. Filenames may include `_New`.

Resolved paths:

- FSD → `pipeline/test-data/Milestone<N>/FSD/<FsdFileName.docx>` (prefer `*_New` when both exist)
- Figma → `pipeline/test-data/Milestone<N>/Figma/<FigmaFileName.html>`
- Excel → `pipeline/test-data/Milestone<N>/Test Cases/<OutputWorkbook.xlsx>`

Stage JSON under `results/fsd-figma-pipeline/<resultsKey>/`.

## Day-to-day UX

1. Add/update files under Milestone`N` `FSD/` and `Figma/` (drop `*_New` beside the original when revising)
2. Tell the agent the **exact FSD + Figma (+ Excel out) filenames** and milestone if not 2 — or name the module and let it prefer `*_New`
3. Agent **creates or reconciles** Excel **and** reports coverage + **feature delta** + TC delta (overall %, modules, features, add/update/retire/keep)
4. Approve Excel when prompted (approves retire list when reconcile)
5. Handoff to `qa-automation-pipeline` → `tests/milestoneN/` (full generate on create; delta sync on reconcile → **specs updated**)

## Workflow

```
Resolve active (+ baseline) FSD/Figma (*_New preference)
  → detect excelMode (create | reconcile)
  → inventories → feature-delta-report → alignment (FSD wins) → use cases
  → [reconcile: parse existing Excel → tc-delta-report]
  → create or in-place patch Excel
  → coverage-matrix.json + stage0-atomicity-report.json + feature-delta-report.json + tc-delta-report.json
  → `npm run fsd:coverage-report` (Feature changes + **Atomicity gate** + Modules + Features + TC delta)
  → [100% coverage + atomicity gates] → [Approve Excel]
  → qa-automation-pipeline (create | reconcile → update specs)
```

## Mandatory coverage + atomicity gates

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Coverage artifact | `results/fsd-figma-pipeline/<resultsKey>/coverage-matrix.json` |
| Atomicity artifact | `results/fsd-figma-pipeline/<resultsKey>/stage0-atomicity-report.json` |
| Validate | `npm run fsd:validate-atomicity -- --results-key "<resultsKey>"` |
| Coverage pass | `coveragePct === 100` and no uncovered requirement IDs |
| Atomicity pass | `atomicityReady === true` — one REQ per use case; `testCaseCount >= inScopeRequirements`; negative/boundary TCs when FSD requires; no compound AC |
| Combined gate | `gateReady = coverage pass AND atomicityReady AND fineGrainReady` |
| Fine-grain pass | `fineGrainReady === true` — `testCaseCount > inScopeRequirements` when Figma slots exist; every composite flow, save, tab, category UI slot has a dedicated TC |
| Roll-ups | `byModule` and `byFeature` **required** |
| Feature delta | `feature-delta-report.json` **required** when `_New` or baseline exists |
| Delta | `tc-delta-report.json` **required** for create and reconcile |
| User message | After every Excel write: run `npm run fsd:coverage-report` (includes atomicity section) and paste full markdown |
| Fail coverage | Gate `BlockedCoverage` |
| Fail atomicity | Gate `BlockedAtomicity` — split bundled TCs; no Approve/handoff |
| Exception | User explicitly accepts gaps → record `userAcceptedGaps` / `userAcceptedAtomicityGaps` |

Traceability: **FSD requirement → use case → Excel TC ID → (after handoff) script**.

## Excel column rules (agents)

- **Task Description** = plain-English, verb-led, single-intent title a non-technical reviewer understands without the FSD (maps from use-case `title`).
- Do **not** put `REQ-*`, `FSD S*`, `BR-*` / `FR-*` / `NFR-*` / `UC-*` IDs, jargon-only wording, or vague “Verify the requirement” into Task Description.
- **Acceptance Criteria** = plain-English measurable pass conditions only.
- Do **not** fill Acceptance Criteria with `REQ-*`, `FSD S*`, or section IDs.
- Keep FSD/requirement traceability in Stage 0 JSON (`use-cases.json`, `coverage-matrix.json`, `tc-delta-report.json`, `feature-delta-report.json`) only — **do not** add a Requirement ID column to Excel.

## Test case design (no bundling)

- **Atomic REQs and TCs** — one primary intent per case; **exactly one `requirementId` per use case**; split FSD multi-behavior bullets.
- **Mechanical gate:** `npm run fsd:validate-atomicity` after every Excel write; `gateReady` requires `atomicityReady`.
- **Create mode:** never read other workbooks in `Test Cases/` — FSD + Figma + use-cases only.
- **Discover** interactive flows from this run’s Figma (modules differ — no fixed flow list).
- **Model flow dependencies** — `navGraph` + `compositeFlows` in html-inventory; `dependsOnUseCaseIds` + `preconditions` in use-cases.json.
- **One happy-path TC** per discovered flow when FSD defines success; **field validations** always separate; validation/save TCs must **Preconditions or steps** evidence prerequisite navigation.
- Do not achieve 100% coverage with a small set of fat multi-intent rows.

## Test Steps (concrete UI only — this run’s Figma)

- Interactive steps come from **this run’s** Figma inventory only (active / `*_New` HTML when used).
- FSD drives Acceptance Criteria / Expected Result.
- When Figma shows a multi-step path, mirror it (open → fill/select → primary action → observe).
- **Dependent flows:** validation/negative rows need Preconditions naming screen/tab state or full chain in Test Steps (audit chain coverage).
- **Forbidden:** placeholders; inventing labels; copying another module’s flows.
- Do not set `AwaitingReview` while placeholder or foreign-module steps remain.

## Protected agents — never modify casually

`test-generator`, `test-healer`; invoke `qa-automation-pipeline` only after Excel approval **and** coverage gate pass (or accepted gaps). Explicit user authorization is required to edit protected agent files.
